<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-11-04T21:59:52Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Netanyahu claims 'serious concerns' of foreign spending to sway Israeli election</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:21c0eefe47f4a72819b6ab4a05f9601af8d6dd11c17aca8fb75c823be269d53e</id><updated>2026-11-04T21:59:52Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T21:26:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261104-netanyahu-claims-serious-concerns-of-foreign-spending-to-sway-israeli-election" /><summary type="html">Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu on Wednesday cited "serious suspicions" around foreign interference in Israel's recent parliamentary elections. He claims foreign countries spent large amounts of money to influence the results, while the largest Arab-Israeli bloc called such accusations "political persecution".</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>South Africans vote in key municipal elections</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:57725a49f333927d5a84ad55358db26392d06b489ac8b7bc56b6d7717ad10e1d</id><updated>2026-11-04T21:59:52Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T21:26:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/south-africans-vote-in-key-municipal-elections" /><summary type="html">In tonight's edition, a crucial test for South Africa's  ruling ANC as millions vote to elect municipal governments. Also, Ethiopia has expelled six Sudanese diplomats amid accusations it's allowing the paramilitary RSF to launch drone strikes from its territory. And a deepening humanitarian crisis in Ethiopia, where renewed fighting has displaced thousands.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Musk-backed candidates lose midterms despite financial backing</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b990a680a8675926ddb86f1f0b1081e4c36c61b8f2194eb2f49b63def00186f0</id><updated>2026-11-04T21:59:52Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T21:06:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/musk-backed-candidates-lose-midterms-despite-financial-backing" /><summary type="html">Shares of Tesla and SpaceX dropped after the Democratic party swept to power in America's midterm elections. Their founder, tech titan Elon Musk, poured over $440 million into Republican candidates and causes, the single biggest campaign donor in the election cycle. But his investment fell flat, as his preferred candidates lost races in Texas, where he has put down roots.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Trump’s second-term playbook: Fake news, AI and attacks on his critics</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:af6bd97788d6a0062458be60cc49981d5adeae55dfe9513bab8402c840eed932</id><updated>2026-11-04T21:59:52Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T20:44:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/truth-or-fake/20261104-trump-s-second-term-playbook-fake-news-ai-and-attacks-on-his-critics" /><summary type="html">Donald Trump could be credited with popularising the term "fake news", but his own presidency has been riddled with numerous false claims, conspiracy theories and misleading content. In this special fact-checking segment, Vedika Bahl examines his Trump's second term: his consistent attacks on political opponents, use of AI-generated images to glorify himself and push political narratives, and what happens when journalists challenge him.</summary><category term="Truth or Fake" /></entry><entry><title>How Chinese AI is censoring the controversy around Mbappé’s Chairman Mao comments</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0eb50798ed6707cf3c8646ddf420caeb1dcc92698ba61fe0720ab51a729e27b5</id><updated>2026-11-04T21:59:52Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T20:28:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261104-how-chinese-ai-is-censoring-the-controversy-around-mbappes-chairman-mao-comments" /><summary type="html">Footballer Kylian Mbappé sparked a wave of condemnation across China when he implied that Chinese leader Mao Zedong was a dictator. In China, information about this controversy is being censored by Chinese AI chatbots.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Blue wave across America: do US midterms signal beginning of the end for Trump?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:032586f39d08902b36e0e3bca1ff1fbc7f8b13e7d481500862a9c5b3a6f9e30a</id><updated>2026-11-04T21:59:52Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T19:49:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261104-blue-wave-across-america-do-us-midterms-signal-beginning-of-the-end-for-trump" /><summary type="html">He asked voters to pretend he was on the ballot and they did. Voters across the United States chasing Donald Trump's Republican majorities from both houses of Congress. How big a landslide for the Democrats?</summary><category term="The Debate" /></entry><entry><title>🔴 Live: Trump says going to war in Iran was worth it, despite midterm rout</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4a29c0056bf012154284136d90e7af443c843bd47bc23315dc87929107a2bd1f</id><updated>2026-11-04T21:59:52Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T18:32:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261103-live-americans-head-to-the-polls-to-vote-in-us-midterm-elections" /></entry><entry><title>Democrats warn Trump camp to ‘lawyer up’ as anger over corruption drives midterms wipeout</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4c06deaa4c90eac46709a75df493d5e468b20e6d9c98f42c97b03d47caba6174</id><updated>2026-11-04T21:59:52Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T18:01:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261104-democrats-warn-trump-camp-lawyer-up-anger-over-corruption-drives-midterms-wipeout-gop" /><summary type="html">Corruption in government was high on the minds of US voters as they dealt US President Donald Trump’s party a chastening defeat in midterm elections, toppling Republican strongholds like dominoes and flipping both chambers of Congress. Triumphant Democrats have warned the Trump administration to “lawyer up”; how they go about tackling alleged graft and abuse of power could shape both their own fortunes and the country’s politics.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>'Once-in-a-generation event: Historic election a shocking repudiation of Trump &amp; the MAGA movement'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:35be95ae0ba79a12d57e3a5e028007eed5fdbbfd6849755fb833dcbc172e1d66</id><updated>2026-11-04T21:59:52Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T17:49:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/once-in-a-generation-event-historic-election-a-shocking-repudiation-of-trump-the-maga-movement" /><summary type="html">Erin Ogunkeye is pleased to welcome Adam Jentleson, President of the Searchlight Institute and author of Supermajority: How Democrats Can Build Lasting Power, For Jentleson, the Democrats' sweeping midterm victory represents far more than the familiar backlash against an incumbent president. "This is a once-in-a-generation event." But electoral breadth presents a governing dilemma. Can a coalition stretching from progressive reformers to culturally conservative Democrats translate its diversity into legislative action? "Pluralism is not just a political strategy. It is actually a moral good in a democracy," he insists. But electoral breadth presents a governing dilemma. Can a coalition stretching from progressive reformers to culturally conservative Democrats translate its diversity into legislative action? And can a party united by opposition to Trump sustain that unity when confronted with difficult choices over healthcare, immigration, economic inequality and climate change?</summary></entry><entry><title>European leaders welcome Democrats' US midterms election win</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8680ec91f3183c20193a82172ee8bf04cb0cb2a8c8f5265ebbdb84257131fe7a</id><updated>2026-11-04T21:59:52Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T17:00:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/european-leaders-welcome-democrats-us-midterms-election-win" /><summary type="html">European leaders voiced hopes for a reset with the United States on Wednesday, November 4, after voters delivered a huge midterm election defeat to President Donald Trump and his Republican party. FRANCE 24's Dave Keating has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>US midterms bring a wave of historic firsts as minorities win key races</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9d88e60c4962c3a7c6455e3628cf8c75dae51308893c81cdfae3aeb450d821e3</id><updated>2026-11-04T21:59:52Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T16:51:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-midterms-bring-a-wave-of-historic-firsts-as-minorities-win-key-races" /><summary type="html">US midterms bring a wave of historic firsts as minorities win key races: The first Native American female senator in Minnesota, the first openly gay male senator in New Hampshire, the first Muslim senator in Michigan and the country's first Black female governor in Georgia. FRANCE 24's Elitsa Gadeva has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>US midterms: Iran's deputy parliament speaker reacts to Trump's elections setback</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5ed57901f74b88becb1c640aec8917bd7758989ff52d0be473e737d3610a577e</id><updated>2026-11-04T21:59:52Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T16:50:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261104-us-midterms-iran-s-deputy-parliament-speaker-reacts-to-trump-s-elections-setback-1" /><summary type="html">First Deputy Speaker of the Parliament of Iran Ali Nikzad on Wednesday attributed Republican losses in the US midterm elections to Washington's war with Iran, telling lawmakers that American efforts to pressure Tehran had failed.  Democrats won control of both chambers of Congress in Tuesday's midterm elections.</summary></entry><entry><title>REPLAY: Senate Democratic leader Chuck Schumer on US midterms</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a7fb0c09fc4fd4de53fffb0fd15502f4b493039d6d8c76f2d8b2c012d35e5cb7</id><updated>2026-11-04T21:59:52Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T16:42:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/replay-senate-democratic-leader-chuck-schumer-on-us-midterms" /><summary type="html">The US Senate Democratic leader Chuck Schumer talked to the press after the midterm election results. Democrats are riding their sweep of Congress into a new era, eager to meet voter demands for change with plans to tackle high costs of living and confront President Donald Trump's final years in the White House.</summary></entry><entry><title>US Midterms: How will Trump manage working with Democrats?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a6fdd55fb89ad4e2b69f3b28fe8ea304d8fab9bd41a747436f3d8ea7cb324650</id><updated>2026-11-04T21:59:52Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T16:24:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-midterms-how-will-trump-manage-working-with-democrats" /><summary type="html">Democrats are riding their sweep of Congress into a new era, eager to meet voter demands for change with plans to tackle high costs of living. How will Donald Trump manage to work with them? FRANCE 24's Ophelie Jacobson has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Tale of 2 midterms: Republican redistricting 'backfired' while Democrats 'exceeded all expectations'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5dca5decba509c6b4eebcfa21bcbd86aac223e8df0c9b454dfc8e265308dea2b</id><updated>2026-11-04T21:59:52Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T16:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tale-of-2-midterms-republican-redistricting-backfired-while-democrats-exceeded-all-expectations" /><summary type="html">Following a resounding Midterm election defeat, Is MAGA Losing Its Grip on the Republican Party? Erin Ogunkeye is pleased to welcome Bryan Lanza, Republican strategist and Partner in Mercury's Washington DC office. "The big thing about MAGA was confrontation, in your face," explained Lanza. But following a veritable blue wave, he believes the electorate has delivered a warning: "We need to move beyond that." While Donald Trump has acknowledged the Democratic victory, at times combative, at times conciliatory, Lanza argues that the president must begin his final two years in office reversing damaging tariffs, addressing widespread dissatisfaction with immigration enforcement and navigating a highly unpopular Iran war.</summary></entry><entry><title>Trump after the midterms: Gridlock, impeachment and succession?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a06497890cb6dcb5c6084c25c5dffa47b51899b01302bacd02da4225989dc3b1</id><updated>2026-11-04T21:59:52Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T15:54:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261104-trump-after-the-midterms-gridlock-impeachment-and-succession" /><summary type="html">Following the US midterms, US President Donald Trump could face a turbulent final two years in office. From budget battles to potential impeachment proceedings, what does the new political balance of power mean for his presidency? FRANCE 24's International Affairs Editor Philip Turle breaks it down.</summary></entry><entry><title>US midterm elections: 'Maybe the best colour for Texas is purple'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4f7a4e6c59df91a7ccfc6bfc481eb9f96b3705a08269ff94bac600f1690f9183</id><updated>2026-11-04T21:59:52Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T15:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-midterm-elections-maybe-the-best-colour-for-texas-is-purple" /><summary type="html">Texas flipped blue following the US midterm elections, marking a historic shift for a state that hasn't been led by Democrats in decades. The legacy of prolonged Republican leadership has left a lasting mark, but as Democrat James Talarico said with this election, 'maybe the best colour for Texas is purple.' FRANCE 24's Texas correspondent Andres Espinal reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>'Is Republican Party able to pivot away from MAGA movement, or will it sputter forward leaderless?'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:166a443e5bbe6f354acf0d2491715cefc72ced0e320e9a5b800784437e70d6f0</id><updated>2026-11-04T21:59:52Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T15:16:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/is-republican-party-able-to-pivot-away-from-maga-movement-or-will-it-sputter-forward-leaderless" /><summary type="html">Does an electoral repudiation of Donald Trump also mark the beginning of MAGA’s decline? Delano D'Souza is pleased to welcome Ian Reifowitz, SUNY Distinguished Professor of Historical Studies at Empire State University, who describes the Republican defeat as “an absolute and complete repudiation” of the president. He connects voters’ economic frustrations with resentment over presidential enrichment, while questioning whether ideological differences between progressive and moderate Democrats proved decisive. Looking towards 2028, Reifowitz identifies a central Republican dilemma: “If JD Vance is the nominee, he can’t run against Donald Trump”, yet Trump himself may refuse to relinquish control of the party.</summary></entry><entry><title>French blood banks foil new cyberattack targeting refrigerators</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c081e9236900e92a7713b1b6e2a3fdfed8b5fdd35c029a55d664efd8c96a83a9</id><updated>2026-11-04T21:59:52Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T15:10:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261104-french-blood-banks-foil-new-cyberattack-targeting-refrigerators" /><summary type="html">A cyberattack in France targeted three cold stores containing donated blood samples and plasma, authorities said on Wednesday. The incident – which was unsuccessful due to the facilities' alarm systems – is the latest in a series of suspected attacks that have targeted refrigerators in European supermarkets, as well as French cooperative bank, Credit Mutuel Arkea, which was also affected Wednesday.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>US midterm elections: Gen Z gives Democrats their strongest support</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ce37c4959dabfb711407b4f084848cc1a17aae8a23b6368b890a6cc805bd69b5</id><updated>2026-11-04T21:59:52Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T15:10:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261104-us-midterm-elections-gen-z-gives-democrats-their-strongest-support" /><summary type="html">In the US midterm elections, 50 million members of Gen Z were eligible to vote. Young voters gave Democrats the strongest support, with 75% of them voting for the party. This generation will be the biggest voting bloc in the United States in the coming years. FRANCE 24's Ophelie Jacobson has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>How Trump's broken promises on war, inflation handed Democrats the midterms</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:08d5aeeeb3efe517536aac85c48ec1f1a071b42ded44922b0b5493d39039f280</id><updated>2026-11-04T21:59:52Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T15:02:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261104-how-trump-s-broken-promises-on-war-inflation-handed-democrats-the-midterms" /><summary type="html">Speaking to Fox News following the midterm elections, US President Donald Trump admitted that inflation was likely one reason Republicans did poorly. Many Americans have been frustrated with how the Iran war has pushed up prices, including at the gasoline pump, especially given that Trump had campaigned for his second term on a pledge of “no new wars”, as Ellen Gainsford explains.</summary></entry><entry><title>Midterms: How Abdul El-Sayed used 'humour and hope' to rebuff racism</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4d1ba87b9cf829198ab08e85eb1de99f31d8aecb900a7e1a1b73823661191bdd</id><updated>2026-11-04T21:59:52Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T14:25:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261104-midterms-how-abdul-el-sayed-used-humour-and-hope-to-rebuff-racism" /><summary type="html">Abdul El-Sayed is set to become the first Muslim senator in US history following his midterms victory in Michigan. His victory came despite what he has denounced as racist attacks against him, inlcuding from Donald Trump, which, says FRANCE 24's correspondent Jessica Le Masurier, he rebuffed with a mixture of "humour and hope".</summary></entry><entry><title>Trump seeks to shift blame but has 'nowhere to hide' after midterms defeat</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e893829383849cd56c44132fa208d21eac46ce1e215ea9ae9242cfc067364dfb</id><updated>2026-11-04T21:59:52Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T14:13:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261104-trump-seeks-to-shift-blame-but-has-nowhere-to-hide-after-midterms-defeat" /><summary type="html">Donald Trump has sought to shift the blame for the Republicans' defeat at the midterms by claiming that if he had been on the ballot the party would have won. But the "blue wave" that saw Democrats win control of Congress can be traced directly back to Trump's decisions, says France 24's Washington correspondent Fraser Jackson.</summary></entry><entry><title>US Midterms: 'It is now going to be pretty chaotic for Donald Trump'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9fc8ca0798b20da646ef433b97225e3c36a662c5aed828d3acde44c700d68c4d</id><updated>2026-11-04T21:59:52Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T14:12:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261104-us-midterms-it-is-now-going-to-be-pretty-chaotic-for-donald-trump" /><summary type="html">The Democrats' victory in the midterm elections have left Donald Trump in a difficult position for the rest of his mandate. The now "blue" House of Representatives will decide the budget, which Trump will have to accept and follow. FRANCE 24's international affairs editor Philip Turle has more.</summary></entry></feed>
